---
import PhotoPlaceholder from '../PhotoPlaceholder.astro';
import VisionFigure from '../VisionFigure.astro';
import SectionHead from '../SectionHead.astro';
---

<section class="band-cream section">
  <SectionHead num="5 / 14 — Place" heading="The Strip is a rehearsal." />

  <div class="container-page">
    <PhotoPlaceholder
      description="A walkable Vegas neighborhood in the won state — apartments above shops, a tree-lined sidewalk, a kid on a bike. Not the Strip. A version of Henderson, Summerlin, or East LV that's allowed to look like a real neighborhood."
    />
  </div>

  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="vision-prose">
      <p>
        The Strip is the densest, most walkable place in the metropolitan United States that almost
        nobody actually lives in. It is also the proof that Las&nbsp;Vegas knows how to build
        mixed-use urbanism — apartments above retail, street-level commerce, foot traffic, transit
        you can rely on, civic life. We just chose to build it for tourists and not for residents.
      </p>
      <p>
        A Saturday in the Valley we're building looks like a quieter, more residential version of
        the Strip's basic logic. A grocery store at the corner. Apartments above it. A park across
        the street. A duplex half a block down, a courtyard fourplex next to it. A school six
        minutes' walk away. The bus stop, ten. None of it looks dense — there are no towers and no
        gridlock — but everyone living here can run their daily errands without getting in a car.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container-page">
    <VisionFigure num="5" title="Five kinds of home">
      <div class="typology">
        <div class="typology-cell is-current">
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 100 100"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            aria-hidden="true"
            ><path d="M22 50 L50 25 L78 50 L78 88 L22 88 Z"></path><rect
              x="36"
              y="60"
              width="28"
              height="22"></rect><line x1="50" y1="60" x2="50" y2="82"></line></svg
          >
          <span class="typology-label">Single-family</span>
        </div>
        <div class="typology-cell is-missing">
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 100 100"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            aria-hidden="true"
            ><path d="M10 52 L26 36 L42 52 L42 88 L10 88 Z"></path><path
              d="M58 52 L74 36 L90 52 L90 88 L58 88 Z"></path><rect
              x="18"
              y="64"
              width="16"
              height="18"></rect><rect x="66" y="64" width="16" height="18"></rect></svg
          >
          <span class="typology-label">Duplex</span>
        </div>
        <div class="typology-cell is-missing">
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 100 100"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            aria-hidden="true"
            ><rect x="20" y="22" width="60" height="66"></rect><line x1="50" y1="22" x2="50" y2="88"
            ></line><line x1="20" y1="55" x2="80" y2="55"></line><rect
              x="29"
              y="68"
              width="10"
              height="20"></rect><rect x="61" y="68" width="10" height="20"></rect><rect
              x="29"
              y="32"
              width="10"
              height="14"></rect><rect x="61" y="32" width="10" height="14"></rect></svg
          >
          <span class="typology-label">Fourplex</span>
        </div>
        <div class="typology-cell is-missing">
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 100 100"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            aria-hidden="true"
            ><path d="M14 30 L14 88 L40 88 L40 56 L60 56 L60 88 L86 88 L86 30 Z"></path><rect
              x="20"
              y="65"
              width="6"
              height="14"></rect><rect x="74" y="65" width="6" height="14"></rect><rect
              x="20"
              y="38"
              width="8"
              height="10"></rect><rect x="36" y="38" width="8" height="10"></rect><rect
              x="56"
              y="38"
              width="8"
              height="10"></rect><rect x="72" y="38" width="8" height="10"></rect></svg
          >
          <span class="typology-label">Courtyard</span>
        </div>
        <div class="typology-cell is-missing">
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 100 100"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            aria-hidden="true"
            ><rect x="14" y="64" width="72" height="24"></rect><rect
              x="14"
              y="40"
              width="72"
              height="24"></rect><rect x="14" y="16" width="72" height="24"></rect><rect
              x="22"
              y="20"
              width="12"
              height="14"></rect><rect x="44" y="20" width="12" height="14"></rect><rect
              x="66"
              y="20"
              width="12"
              height="14"></rect><rect x="22" y="44" width="12" height="14"></rect><rect
              x="44"
              y="44"
              width="12"
              height="14"></rect><rect x="66" y="44" width="12" height="14"></rect><rect
              x="22"
              y="68"
              width="34"
              height="16"></rect><rect x="62" y="68" width="16" height="16"></rect></svg
          >
          <span class="typology-label">Mixed-use</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Fragment slot="caption">
        Most of the Valley today only allows the first one. The other four — what urbanists call
        <em>missing-middle housing</em> — are illegal in most neighborhoods. Not because Vegas doesn't
        want them. Because the zoning rules say no.
      </Fragment>
    </VisionFigure>
  </div>

  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="vision-prose">
      <p>
        Most of the Valley today only allows the first kind of building above: the single-family
        detached home with a yard. The other four — duplexes, fourplexes, courtyard apartments,
        mixed-use buildings — are illegal in most neighborhoods. They're not missing because Vegas
        forgot how to build them. They're missing because the zoning rules, most of which haven't
        been seriously revised since the 1960s, say no.
      </p>
      <p>
        The fix is not to demolish anything. It's to allow what comes next to be built — a fourplex
        on a teardown lot, an ADU in a backyard, a corner store where one used to exist sixty years
        ago. Stretched across the Valley, that produces real town centers in Henderson, Summerlin,
        North Las&nbsp;Vegas, downtown, around UNLV. Not one Strip surrounded by cul-de-sacs, but a
        metro that looks and works like the metros people leave Las&nbsp;Vegas to visit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container-page">
    <VisionFigure num="6" title="A Valley with many centers">
      <svg
        class="valley-map"
        viewBox="0 0 600 360"
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Stylized map of the Las Vegas Valley showing town centers in Henderson, Summerlin, North Las Vegas, downtown, and around UNLV, connected by transit corridors"
      >
        <path
          class="valley-bound"
          d="M80 200 Q110 120, 200 90 Q320 70, 440 95 Q520 130, 530 220 Q525 290, 460 320 Q360 340, 250 330 Q140 320, 95 270 Z"
        ></path>
        <text class="valley-axis" x="60" y="130">Spring Mts</text>
        <text class="valley-axis" x="510" y="270">Sunrise Mts</text>
        <text class="valley-axis" x="280" y="60">Sheep Range</text>
        <text class="valley-axis" x="280" y="350">McCullough</text>
        <circle class="valley-ring" cx="290" cy="200" r="28"></circle><circle
          class="valley-dot-accent"
          cx="290"
          cy="200"
          r="6"></circle>
        <text class="valley-center" x="290" y="187" text-anchor="middle">Downtown</text>
        <circle class="valley-ring" cx="305" cy="240" r="22"></circle><circle
          class="valley-dot-accent"
          cx="305"
          cy="240"
          r="5"></circle>
        <text class="valley-center" x="305" y="262" text-anchor="middle">Strip · UNLV</text>
        <circle class="valley-ring" cx="430" cy="270" r="20"></circle><circle
          class="valley-dot"
          cx="430"
          cy="270"
          r="5"></circle>
        <text class="valley-center" x="430" y="295" text-anchor="middle">Henderson</text>
        <circle class="valley-ring" cx="160" cy="180" r="20"></circle><circle
          class="valley-dot"
          cx="160"
          cy="180"
          r="5"></circle>
        <text class="valley-center" x="160" y="167" text-anchor="middle">Summerlin</text>
        <circle class="valley-ring" cx="280" cy="135" r="20"></circle><circle
          class="valley-dot"
          cx="280"
          cy="135"
          r="5"></circle>
        <text class="valley-center" x="280" y="122" text-anchor="middle">North&nbsp;LV</text>
        <circle class="valley-ring" cx="395" cy="200" r="18"></circle><circle
          class="valley-dot"
          cx="395"
          cy="200"
          r="5"></circle>
        <text class="valley-center" x="395" y="187" text-anchor="middle">Sunrise</text>
        <circle class="valley-ring" cx="220" cy="240" r="18"></circle><circle
          class="valley-dot"
          cx="220"
          cy="240"
          r="5"></circle>
        <text class="valley-center" x="220" y="262" text-anchor="middle">Spring Valley</text>
        <path class="valley-corridor" d="M280 135 Q285 175, 290 200"></path>
        <path class="valley-corridor" d="M290 200 L395 200"></path>
        <path class="valley-corridor" d="M305 240 Q360 260, 430 270"></path>
        <path class="valley-corridor" d="M290 200 Q220 195, 160 180"></path>
        <path class="valley-corridor" d="M290 200 Q255 220, 220 240"></path>
      </svg>
      <Fragment slot="caption">
        Today, the Valley has one big destination: the Strip. The won Valley has many — real town
        centers across the metro, each a place where people live, work, shop, and connect. Dotted
        lines mark the next decade's transit spine.
      </Fragment>
    </VisionFigure>
  </div>

  <div class="container-narrow">
    <p class="vision-tail">
      The Strip already proves it works in Vegas. We just want it where we live.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .typology {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: end;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .typology {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      gap: 1.5rem 1rem;
    }
  }
  .typology-cell {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .typology-cell svg {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 110px;
    height: auto;
    color: var(--vp-text);
  }
  .typology-label {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .typology-cell.is-current {
    opacity: 0.42;
  }
  .typology-cell.is-current .typology-label::after {
    content: ' (today)';
    color: var(--vp-text-muted);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }
  .typology-cell.is-missing svg {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .valley-map {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-height: 360px;
  }
  .valley-bound {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 4%, transparent);
    stroke: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 24%, transparent);
    stroke-width: 1;
    stroke-dasharray: 4 5;
  }
  .valley-ring {
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1.2;
    opacity: 0.18;
  }
  .valley-dot {
    fill: currentColor;
  }
  .valley-dot-accent {
    fill: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .valley-center {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 700;
    fill: currentColor;
  }
  .valley-axis {
    font-size: 9px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--vp-text-muted);
  }
  .valley-corridor {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-accent);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
    stroke-dasharray: 2 4;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }
</style>
